# kinhin

> Autoscaling CI runners that live on your Mac — ephemeral, resource-aware, and gone when the job is done. macOS jobs run on Tart VMs; Linux jobs on apple/container microVMs, Docker containers, or Tart Linux VMs.

**The mindful CI**

- **In beta**: GitHub, Gitea, Forgejo and GitLab CE are supported. Gitea, Forgejo and GitLab CE run end to end on every runtime in kinhin's own test suite; GitHub has run on Tart macOS VMs and apple/container. Buildkite, Azure Pipelines and Bitbucket are planned. <a href="/guide/forges#what-has-been-tested">What has been tested</a> · <a href="/guide/beta-roadmap">Roadmap to v0.1.0</a> [undefined](https://kinhin.dev/v0.0.1-beta-1undefined.md)
- **Real concurrency**: Self-hosted runners handle one job at a time. Kinhin scales a fleet of ephemeral runners to your queue so jobs run in parallel. <a href="/guide/why-kinhin">Why kinhin</a> [undefined](https://kinhin.dev/v0.0.1-beta-1undefined.md)
- **Ephemeral by default**: Every job gets a fresh VM or container. The runner deregisters itself afterwards and the instance is deleted — no state leaks between jobs. [undefined](https://kinhin.dev/v0.0.1-beta-1undefined.md)
- **Multi-forge**: GitHub Actions, GitLab CI/CD, Gitea Actions and Forgejo Actions served from one shared pool. Buildkite, Azure Pipelines and Bitbucket Pipelines are planned. [undefined](https://kinhin.dev/v0.0.1-beta-1undefined.md)
- **Multi-runtime**: macOS jobs on Tart VMs, Linux jobs on apple/container microVMs, Docker containers, or Tart Linux VMs — each job routed by repo, workflow, or runs-on label. [undefined](https://kinhin.dev/v0.0.1-beta-1undefined.md)
- **Resource-aware**: The scaler never exceeds what your Mac can handle. Host CPU, memory, and disk headroom are always reserved, and the budget is partitioned across runtime pools. [undefined](https://kinhin.dev/v0.0.1-beta-1undefined.md)
- **Menu bar or headless**: The same engine behind a macOS menu bar app or a LaunchAgent daemon — same config, either way, exactly one fleet. [undefined](https://kinhin.dev/v0.0.1-beta-1undefined.md)
- **One-line install**: curl … \| bash from GitHub Releases with sha256 verification, no Gatekeeper dance, and a clean uninstall. [undefined](https://kinhin.dev/v0.0.1-beta-1undefined.md)

